WEBVTT

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:07.160
Inside a sealed-off house...

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.860
the ultimate deception game begins.

00:00:15.831 --> 00:00:23.321
And presiding over it are... / these two.

00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:25.421
All right, Ninomiya. / Yeah.

00:00:25.721 --> 00:00:29.141
At last, the feast begins. / That's right.

00:00:29.281 --> 00:00:35.761
Eight players. Which one will survive? /
Shall we begin?

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:39.081
Yes. / Let the ultimate mind game begin.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:42.901
It's me. / It's me.

00:00:43.441 --> 00:00:44.601
What a sneaky face.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.601
Inside this house,

00:00:48.511 --> 00:00:56.401
there are three forbidden NG actions you
must never do.

00:00:58.361 --> 00:01:01.842
Anyone who triggers three NGs... / Hold
on.

00:01:01.982 --> 00:01:03.482
is immediately eliminated. / In this
world.

00:01:03.482 --> 00:01:04.482
Two players just got an NG. / Huh?

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:11.202
Rely only on the warning tone that sounds
when someone triggers an NG,

00:01:11.282 --> 00:01:13.202
and deduce what the NGs are.

00:01:14.602 --> 00:01:18.902
The second someone said “three,” it went
off, so maybe saying numbers? / Ohhh.

00:01:18.962 --> 00:01:19.962
Ah!

00:01:19.982 --> 00:01:26.662
Whoever figures it out first can bait
rivals who still do not know into triggering an NG and knock them out.

00:01:27.382 --> 00:01:31.102
Survival. / He is trying to make him take
off his jacket!

00:01:31.542 --> 00:01:33.962
How many times before you are out? / Eiko
Kano nailed him just now!

00:01:35.602 --> 00:01:39.502
The ultimate deception game begins now.

00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:47.543
Players, please gather in the playroom. /
All right.

00:01:47.543 --> 00:01:53.203
Let's go. / Okay.

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:55.303
Huh? / Oh.

00:01:56.103 --> 00:01:57.043
Oh? / Ohhh.

00:01:57.043 --> 00:02:00.103
They're all in white. / Nice to meet you.

00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:03.423
Nice to meet you. / Looking forward to
this.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.563
Nice to meet you. / Nice to meet you.

00:02:05.563 --> 00:02:07.163
Nice to meet you. / What?

00:02:07.503 --> 00:02:08.563
What a lineup. / What a lineup.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:14.883
All right, shall we greet the players? /
Let us. Yes.

00:02:15.293 --> 00:02:16.293
Short hair. / Becky.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.983
Staff? / Ohhh.

00:02:18.983 --> 00:02:19.983
Everyone... / You scared me!

00:02:20.563 --> 00:02:23.964
Welcome to Secret NG House. / Huh?

00:02:24.044 --> 00:02:25.584
Oh? / NG House?

00:02:25.824 --> 00:02:30.604
From this moment on, all of you will take
part in the ultimate mind game.

00:02:30.904 --> 00:02:36.244
The last person remaining will win prize
money. / What?!

00:02:36.444 --> 00:02:40.124
And here it is. / Let's go!

00:02:40.944 --> 00:02:43.904
Wha, wha, what? / It is moving!

00:02:44.984 --> 00:02:45.544
Whoa! / One, two, three, four...

00:02:45.544 --> 00:02:46.844
What? What? What? / Five million!

00:02:47.244 --> 00:02:47.904
What?! / Half a billion?!

00:02:47.904 --> 00:02:49.544
Is this really five hundred million? / No
way.

00:02:49.564 --> 00:02:55.624
This is insane! / Depending on how the
game unfolds, it could go even higher.

00:02:56.744 --> 00:03:00.864
What?! / Anyway, take down the other
players and claim the prize money.

00:03:01.084 --> 00:03:04.865
So it is head-to-head. / We wish you luck.

00:03:05.405 --> 00:03:06.865
Wait, that is it? / That is it?

00:03:07.085 --> 00:03:09.165
What?

00:03:12.465 --> 00:03:15.845
We will now explain the rules. / We need
to hear this.

00:03:15.925 --> 00:03:19.085
Once the game begins, the playroom you are
in

00:03:19.905 --> 00:03:24.585
will be assigned hidden forbidden actions
called secret NGs.

00:03:26.245 --> 00:03:29.085
What? / If you trigger three NGs, you are
out.

00:03:29.665 --> 00:03:35.405
Wow. / The final player left standing wins
every last yen of the prize money.

00:03:36.685 --> 00:03:43.526
So it is not split evenly. / Also, the
secret NGs are set by the game masters, Ninomiya and Wakabayashi.

00:03:44.006 --> 00:03:45.826
I see. / So those two come up with them.

00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:49.986
You must act while trying to deduce what
the NGs are.

00:03:49.986 --> 00:03:53.346
Man, the NGs those two come up with are
going to be nasty.

00:03:54.206 --> 00:03:59.466
The First Stage will begin shortly. / All
right!

00:03:59.566 --> 00:04:01.886
Players, please return to your rooms once.

00:04:09.666 --> 00:04:12.726
So what should the First Stage secret NGs
be?

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:18.107
Now then, Ninomiya and Wakabayashi set
secret NGs

00:04:18.887 --> 00:04:20.867
to test the brains of all eight players.

00:04:23.307 --> 00:04:28.468
What do you think? Maybe something verbal
and something physical? / Right, right. A movement-based one too.

00:04:28.488 --> 00:04:33.428
But we need them moving, and there are
still a lot of players, so we want to see some NGs happen.

00:04:33.548 --> 00:04:36.409
Yeah, we do. / So maybe a word that comes
up a lot.

00:04:37.089 --> 00:04:38.469
Like numbers. / Ah, right, right.

00:04:39.109 --> 00:04:42.549
Like saying “one.” / Some people might
catch on right away.

00:04:42.729 --> 00:04:45.009
Yeah, I want to see that too. / Yeah.

00:04:45.449 --> 00:04:49.170
Okay, then let us go with that. / Oh, look
at the table.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:53.750
Water and snacks. / Chocolate and gummies.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.811
That is suspicious as hell. / I want to
see the battle over those, though.

00:04:59.651 --> 00:05:02.511
Like not eating at all, not drinking
water... / Or seeing who goes for it first.

00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:07.852
But if it goes off on the first bite, it
will be obvious that eating candy is the NG, right?

00:05:07.892 --> 00:05:09.892
Then nobody will do it anymore.

00:05:10.672 --> 00:05:13.632
What if eating two or more is the NG? /
Oh, that is good.

00:05:13.792 --> 00:05:15.112
So two pieces is out. / And the third one?

00:05:16.532 --> 00:05:21.073
A fist pump? / A fist pump. Something like
that.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:25.913
I feel like someone would trigger an NG
and then do a fist pump.

00:05:26.413 --> 00:05:29.474
Like when someone trying to set a trap
pulls it off. / Right, right, right.

00:05:29.494 --> 00:05:32.394
Ah, we have got to watch for that too. /
Like that side could start popping off as well.

00:05:33.794 --> 00:05:37.634
These eight have no way of knowing what
NGs were set.

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:43.555
Who will be the first to figure one out
and take control of the game?

00:05:43.635 --> 00:05:49.556
I think I can do this. / It is going to
feel amazing when I knock someone out.

00:05:50.756 --> 00:05:54.116
I can win. / I want to make lots of people
trigger NGs.

00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:57.536
Everyone except Matsumaru looked like easy
pickings to me.

00:05:58.016 --> 00:06:03.917
At five million yen, things definitely
change. / I absolutely do not want to lose.

00:06:03.917 --> 00:06:08.757
Kasuga with prize money on the line is
unbeatable. / Now I am getting excited!

00:06:08.797 --> 00:06:15.658
I cannot wait for the First Stage. / All
right, let us begin.

00:06:17.298 --> 00:06:20.899
Players, please gather in the playroom.

00:06:26.039 --> 00:06:28.159
Okay, okay, okay. / Ohh.

00:06:28.599 --> 00:06:30.840
Huh? / What happened to all that
confidence?

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.980
That was weird. Nothing happened. / Wait,
what? What?

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:38.560
Three secret NGs have now been set. / I
see.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.261
First Stage, begin.

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:48.281
Why is everyone stepping back once? / Ah,
so there are three things already...

00:06:49.281 --> 00:06:56.222
Yamazaki. / One just went off.

00:06:57.922 --> 00:06:59.902
Two players triggered an NG. / Ah, two
people got hit.

00:07:02.483 --> 00:07:09.423
An NG already. / Why is everyone stepping
back once?

00:07:10.343 --> 00:07:14.184
So there are three of them, right? / They
have already been set, right?

00:07:15.404 --> 00:07:22.205
Yamazaki, Yashiki, NG 1. / Yashiki and
Yamazaki got one.

00:07:23.005 --> 00:07:25.705
Huh? / What happened?

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.465
What just happened? / Wait, wait.

00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:30.745
The same thing. / Let us calm down.

00:07:30.745 --> 00:07:36.266
But they might not have done the same
thing. / They could each have triggered different NGs.

00:07:36.326 --> 00:07:39.406
Different NGs. / They have barely said
more than two words.

00:07:39.806 --> 00:07:42.326
Ah, I got it. / Who was it?

00:07:44.647 --> 00:07:45.887
Michopa said it. / I cannot do anything.

00:07:45.987 --> 00:07:48.847
Wait a second. / This world is impossible.
It is impossible to live in this world.

00:07:49.407 --> 00:07:50.647
Two players triggered an NG. / Two more
just got hit.

00:07:51.347 --> 00:07:55.268
Ah, two again. / What sound was that?

00:07:56.268 --> 00:08:01.668
We are now reviewing the number of players
who triggered an NG. / Please wait a moment.

00:08:01.928 --> 00:08:02.968
All right, time for deliberation.

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:09.209
They are dropping like flies. As expected.
Classic Wakabayashi. Wakabayashi said a number.

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.509
So repeating it gets you too.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:18.930
To avoid mistakes in the NG ruling, eight
judges review it again in the monitoring room.

00:08:22.906 --> 00:08:24.226
Wait a second. / The same thing.

00:08:25.646 --> 00:08:30.306
But they might not have done the same
thing. / They could each have triggered different NGs.

00:08:30.406 --> 00:08:31.886
Different NGs. / There are three of them,
after all.

00:08:32.006 --> 00:08:38.587
They have barely spoken more than two
words. / True.

00:08:39.607 --> 00:08:40.767
Wait a second. / I cannot do anything.

00:08:40.907 --> 00:08:43.767
Wait a second. / This world is impossible.
It is impossible to live in this world.

00:08:44.307 --> 00:08:45.427
Two players triggered an NG. / Huh? Two
players?

00:08:46.847 --> 00:08:48.727
Did they say it? / They did.

00:08:51.027 --> 00:08:52.567
Not two players. Four players triggered an
NG.

00:08:59.187 --> 00:09:03.447
Four players. / Everyone, please return to
your private rooms.

00:09:05.328 --> 00:09:07.308
That was fast, fast, fast.

00:09:11.648 --> 00:09:17.248
I have no idea. / Wait a second.

00:09:19.628 --> 00:09:22.468
No, but...

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:28.428
When Kano stepped back too,

00:09:28.528 --> 00:09:33.189
it went off, so I feel like stepping back
might be the NG. / But that is impossible.

00:09:33.789 --> 00:09:39.469
They probably still do not know yet. /
When the first NG went off, it said two players, right?

00:09:40.669 --> 00:09:46.089
At that point I mostly only remember
myself, but... / I think two people had their hands clasped behind their backs,

00:09:48.969 --> 00:09:52.869
if I remember right. / So right now I have
two possibilities.

00:09:53.229 --> 00:09:54.969
Oh? / One is...

00:09:55.989 --> 00:09:59.489
when the chocolate came out, / someone
said it looked suspicious.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.710
Yeah. / I do not remember who said it,
though.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.630
And the second is, / me and Kasuga

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.450
had our hands on our hips like this. /
Right.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:08.790
I think it is an action. / Yeah.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:13.230
Because I feel like it went off right
then. / Yeah.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:16.450
If I had to guess... / numbers.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:21.230
Oh. / Like “the last one,” or “there are
two right now.”

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.810
Numbers? / Numbers or pointing.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:27.610
Whoa, that is good. / Kano, that is
actually impressive.

00:10:28.051 --> 00:10:29.811
That could be it. / Man.

00:10:29.811 --> 00:10:31.451
I think I have got it. / Really?

00:10:32.251 --> 00:10:34.851
Can I say it? / There was a word

00:10:35.731 --> 00:10:37.431
that three people said. / Whoa.

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:40.091
Maybe saying “NG” is itself an NG. / Ah.

00:10:41.731 --> 00:10:46.131
Yeah, they are definitely trying to mess
with us. / All right, he is already on the brink.

00:10:46.911 --> 00:10:49.291
This guy. / But surely just talking cannot
be one,

00:10:49.491 --> 00:10:53.751
so I think it is either laughing or
pointing. / Yeah.

00:10:53.791 --> 00:10:55.832
Those are the two I have narrowed it down
to. / Yeah.

00:10:56.472 --> 00:10:57.472
Careful. / So no more laughing.

00:10:57.472 --> 00:10:58.972
Hang in there. / So that means no more
laughing.

00:10:59.392 --> 00:11:01.652
Absolutely. / She pointed.

00:11:01.652 --> 00:11:04.672
Ah. / I did point, though.

00:11:05.052 --> 00:11:09.212
Maybe I should use that next.

00:11:11.852 --> 00:11:15.352
I started thinking I might have triggered
an NG too. / I see, I see.

00:11:15.532 --> 00:11:16.632
You did. / Go ahead.

00:11:17.072 --> 00:11:20.472
There was water on the table, and, like, /
candy too, right?

00:11:21.532 --> 00:11:23.333
And / saying it looked suspicious

00:11:23.753 --> 00:11:28.493
might be the NG, I think. / So do not say
“suspicious.”

00:11:28.873 --> 00:11:31.433
But that is a properly objective read. /
Yeah, true.

00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:36.973
Kano has already started to catch on. /
Can he use

00:11:37.833 --> 00:11:40.313
that advantage to steer his rivals into an
NG?

00:11:42.953 --> 00:11:45.493
Everyone, please return to the playroom.

00:11:47.853 --> 00:11:52.254
This might end before anyone even eats the
candy. / Nobody wants to.

00:11:52.614 --> 00:11:55.554
Everybody is scared of it now. / Look,
nobody is talking anymore.

00:11:55.974 --> 00:11:57.914
The game resumes. / Nobody is talking.

00:11:58.194 --> 00:11:59.974
They were all having so much fun a minute
ago. / This is scary.

00:12:00.434 --> 00:12:01.334
Listen to what they say. / This is scary.

00:12:01.334 --> 00:12:05.074
Even Becky has that look on her face. / I
am not even looking at Becky anymore.

00:12:12.818 --> 00:12:16.659
Let us deliberately go around / and do
self-introductions,

00:12:16.779 --> 00:12:18.339
starting from number one. / Becky first,
maybe?

00:12:18.639 --> 00:12:21.799
Ah, right, we can decide that ourselves
too. / There was never any order set.

00:12:22.559 --> 00:12:23.719
Self-introductions. / Starting with Becky.

00:12:23.739 --> 00:12:27.179
Yeah, I can totally see someone saying
that. / No...

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.280
I think that is bait, guys. / Yeah.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:35.420
Ah, I like the way Ueda's getting
suspicious. / Shall we do it?

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.690
Yeah. / As expected.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:39.040
Mm-hm. / Who should go first?

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:41.701
Let's do it. / Ah, let's go clockwise.
I'll start.

00:12:41.741 --> 00:12:42.981
In order, from one. / From one.

00:12:43.481 --> 00:12:45.641
Start from one? / By room number.

00:12:45.861 --> 00:12:50.181
Kasuga, Kasuga. / Kasuga might go down.

00:12:50.281 --> 00:12:52.722
Yeah. / Ah, but...

00:12:52.862 --> 00:12:53.862
Two players triggered an NG.

00:12:56.862 --> 00:13:00.682
Lured in by the game masters pushing
self-introductions,

00:13:02.742 --> 00:13:05.603
'Let's go clockwise. I'll start.' / 'In
order, from one.'

00:13:06.083 --> 00:13:07.803
Start from one? / By room number.

00:13:09.083 --> 00:13:11.943
Kasuga and Michopa fall right into the
trap. / That makes NG 2.

00:13:11.943 --> 00:13:15.243
One more and they are eliminated.

00:13:15.464 --> 00:13:21.724
He was pointing like this, so / I think
that movement might be Kasuga’s.

00:13:22.344 --> 00:13:24.624
Ah, so... / He is nodding already.

00:13:24.904 --> 00:13:27.364
Michopa’s / thing was this...

00:13:29.085 --> 00:13:31.105
How many times before you are out? /
Three.

00:13:31.625 --> 00:13:35.745
Ah! / Kano just pointed, right now.

00:13:35.865 --> 00:13:40.466
He pointed. / Kano pointed.

00:13:40.526 --> 00:13:43.706
One player triggered an NG. / An
elimination. An elimination.

00:13:45.506 --> 00:13:48.886
Eiko Kano went in for the kill. / Kano
totally knows what it is.

00:13:48.986 --> 00:13:53.367
Scary, scary. Seriously scary. / I have
completely figured out this game.

00:13:53.387 --> 00:13:54.467
Eiko Kano... / Scary.

00:13:55.327 --> 00:13:57.067
Eiko Kano is good at these kinds of games.
/ Yeah.

00:13:57.167 --> 00:13:59.067
No way, no way. / Right.

00:14:00.187 --> 00:14:01.067
Wait. / Huh?

00:14:01.067 --> 00:14:06.828
He is good at games, so now that it is
like this... / Michopa is out already.

00:14:07.688 --> 00:14:13.528
No, Eiko Kano has this game completely in
his hands. / He has taken control of the game.

00:14:14.508 --> 00:14:15.729
No way. / No way.

00:14:17.529 --> 00:14:22.309
And Kano is basically confirmed now,
because he went in pointing. / How many was it again? See?

00:14:22.389 --> 00:14:25.709
He pointed, see? See? / What a sneaky
face.

00:14:25.849 --> 00:14:26.929
He left without saying his name. / Even
though he...

00:14:26.929 --> 00:14:29.370
Actually... / Wait, did someone just talk?

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:33.030
Wait, Michopa did not even do anything. /
No, but if we do not do self-introductions, everyone...

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:36.750
Please return to your private rooms. /
Man...

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:40.351
Wow, that is amazing. / From someone
unexpected, too.

00:14:41.031 --> 00:14:43.651
I had a hunch numbers might be an NG,

00:14:44.931 --> 00:14:48.071
so I deliberately baited people with
numbers.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.003
I don't want to get taken out by Eiko. /
Yeah, nobody wants Eiko to get them.

00:14:52.292 --> 00:14:54.132
Right. / I think he is right.

00:14:54.192 --> 00:14:56.472
Yeah. / I think he is right.

00:14:56.572 --> 00:15:00.112
Yeah, that has to be it. Once he figures
it out... / Kano is going to keep going now.

00:15:00.332 --> 00:15:03.072
Yeah. / I thought I was only one strike
in, but...

00:15:04.293 --> 00:15:08.833
So it really was numbers? / Numbers really
did...

00:15:09.093 --> 00:15:12.313
I got completely played by Kano. / Damn
it!

00:15:12.493 --> 00:15:15.193
Yeah. They are gone, gone. / Gone, gone.

00:15:15.454 --> 00:15:16.854
Man, this is bad. / He is strong.

00:15:17.434 --> 00:15:22.354
I still do not know whether the way I
asked just now was smart or clumsy.

00:15:22.514 --> 00:15:26.974
Because by now, everyone must have
realized numbers are dangerous.

00:15:26.974 --> 00:15:33.515
Kano specifically asked, “How many times
before you are eliminated?”

00:15:33.515 --> 00:15:38.735
And when Michopa answered “three,” she got
eliminated, so...

00:15:40.296 --> 00:15:44.376
yeah, it has to be numbers. / Kano, you
actually played that badly.

00:15:47.096 --> 00:15:50.156
The timing stood out too much because he
pointed.

00:15:51.136 --> 00:15:56.777
If Kano spotted that and baited her on
purpose, then he is terrifying.

00:15:58.217 --> 00:16:00.397
He is seriously strong. / No, he is scary.
He is strong.

00:16:00.437 --> 00:16:04.958
From here on out, if Kano says anything, I
might have to ignore him.

00:16:05.578 --> 00:16:10.498
If they are making us do
self-introductions, then...

00:16:11.398 --> 00:16:16.099
there might be NG actions that naturally
come up during self-introductions too.

00:16:17.399 --> 00:16:21.439
For now I decided not to raise my hand or
anything. / That is where I am at.

00:16:21.699 --> 00:16:26.120
Ah, so close. / I keep thinking about what
exactly Michopa did before now.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:33.120
I seriously have no memory of what Michopa
did. / I do not know.

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.401
I really do not know. / This is bad.

00:16:34.401 --> 00:16:38.021
Like, where you look... / No, I mean,
pointing...

00:16:38.621 --> 00:16:41.341
At first I thought / even that might be
out.

00:16:42.201 --> 00:16:46.542
When Becky and them did something and it
buzzed, I thought,

00:16:47.002 --> 00:16:49.582
ah, maybe pointing at something is the NG.

00:16:49.742 --> 00:16:54.143
Then later someone asked, “How many
strikes is it again?”

00:16:55.923 --> 00:17:00.563
and when she said “three,” it buzzed, so I
thought maybe moving fingers was it, but then Michopa, who had nothing to do with that,

00:17:01.483 --> 00:17:06.384
got taken out, / so maybe I am actually
back to not knowing anything at all.

00:17:06.404 --> 00:17:10.984
Yamazaki, Ueda, and Yashiki are being
targeted. / Totally targeted.

00:17:12.164 --> 00:17:15.185
I know what the NG is now. / Bring it on.

00:17:15.985 --> 00:17:21.405
Yeah, I think saying numbers is probably
in there too. / I might have already gotten one.

00:17:21.405 --> 00:17:23.165
Oh. / Then I better watch the numbers.

00:17:23.225 --> 00:17:29.046
Yeah, anyway, anything involving numbers,
and maybe hands too, like... / room numbers, numbers in general.

00:17:29.566 --> 00:17:34.407
Kasuga gets seriously strong when money is
on the line. / Seriously.

00:17:35.347 --> 00:17:40.247
I have seen him turn the whole room into
absolute chaos so many times. / Beating guys like Fuku Suzuki,

00:17:40.667 --> 00:17:43.547
No, no, this is bad. / and walking off
with like 100,000 yen.

00:17:45.248 --> 00:17:49.988
The second someone said “three,” it went
off, / so maybe it is saying numbers or sticking your hand out or something like that.

00:17:49.988 --> 00:17:51.202
Man, at this point... /
self-introductions...

00:17:52.128 --> 00:17:57.889
because self-intros often involve numbers,
like “I have two kids,” or things like that. / These people...

00:17:57.909 --> 00:18:02.129
Next I want to draw out both numbers and
words somehow. / Oh.

00:18:02.129 --> 00:18:09.110
So he has moved to the baiting side now. /
Wow, so now Kasuga, Kano, Becky, and Matsumaru just will not say numbers.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:13.490
Yeah. / And the rest of this group is
going to try to make them say them from here on out.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:17.771
So they are going to bait each other now.
/ Players, please return to the playroom.

00:18:18.171 --> 00:18:24.952
If Yashiki and Kasuga get baited into it,
/ it will be over right there.

00:18:26.232 --> 00:18:29.792
The game resumes. / Kasuga has figured it
out, so he will not say it. He will not.

00:18:30.012 --> 00:18:32.932
Which means Yashiki is the one here... /
Yeah.

00:18:33.833 --> 00:18:36.853
Here it comes. / Go ahead and introduce
yourselves.

00:18:37.353 --> 00:18:40.193
Yeah. / Here comes the war over numbers.

00:18:41.873 --> 00:18:46.334
And Kano knows it already, so Kano too...
/ Oh, he wants to go in.

00:18:48.314 --> 00:18:52.234
Should we just do the self-intros first?
We know already. / Want to do introductions?

00:18:54.015 --> 00:18:55.635
Yeah. / Yeah.

00:18:58.475 --> 00:19:00.695
Who first? / Why do not we start with the
younger ones?

00:19:00.715 --> 00:19:02.055
Ah, good idea. / How old are you?

00:19:03.015 --> 00:19:04.176
I am 19. / Sorry.

00:19:07.936 --> 00:19:09.736
Ah! / Damn it!

00:19:09.916 --> 00:19:11.516
Ah, come on! / Ah, Becky!

00:19:11.976 --> 00:19:13.377
Scary. / Scary!

00:19:13.717 --> 00:19:14.997
One player triggered an NG. / She's 19.

00:19:15.537 --> 00:19:19.457
Now even Ten must have noticed. / Scary.

00:19:19.537 --> 00:19:21.617
She noticed, she noticed. / Like, “Ah, I
got played.”

00:19:21.737 --> 00:19:23.578
Even Ten. / Has everyone noticed now?

00:19:25.188 --> 00:19:26.188
Nineteen... / Ah.

00:19:28.178 --> 00:19:31.638
Yashiki! / That is why!

00:19:32.098 --> 00:19:35.999
One player triggered an NG. / An
elimination.

00:19:36.399 --> 00:19:39.199
An elimination. / That was close!

00:19:40.719 --> 00:19:43.960
So Ten ended up being saved by that. /
Right.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:47.760
What a dramatic guy. / Seriously.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.180
Pretending not to notice there...

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:55.681
because if he had started and said
“forty-six,” he would have been gone on the spot. / Right.

00:19:56.541 --> 00:20:02.962
Handsome Yashiki saves the day. / Yashiki
did it.

00:20:05.862 --> 00:20:07.922
Becky!

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:16.171
That sort of thing sticks with you. It
stays with you to the end. / One more left.

00:20:16.951 --> 00:20:20.611
One more person gets eliminated. / But
then, who still has not figured it out?

00:20:20.691 --> 00:20:22.591
This one? / Ten noticed, right?

00:20:22.631 --> 00:20:24.511
Probably. I think she knows now. / Should
we do self-introductions?

00:20:24.731 --> 00:20:27.072
It is Ueda, right? / Which number do you
want to go in the self-intros?

00:20:27.072 --> 00:20:29.612
Which number? / Pick someone.

00:20:29.692 --> 00:20:31.572
Then... / I am Yamazaki Ten.

00:20:31.592 --> 00:20:34.453
Nice to meet you. / Ah, she did not say
it.

00:20:34.553 --> 00:20:36.693
Nice to meet you. / So she has figured it
out.

00:20:36.853 --> 00:20:39.913
Ueda noticed. / What year were you born?

00:20:39.913 --> 00:20:41.193
Ah, 2005. / Ah, oh!

00:20:42.334 --> 00:20:45.854
No, no, no, no. / Wait, you had not
realized?

00:20:45.874 --> 00:20:48.594
She had not realized. / I mean, 2005 is
still...

00:20:49.654 --> 00:20:51.075
One player triggered an NG. / An
elimination.

00:20:51.075 --> 00:20:56.535
An elimination. / Because the adults were
not saying anything!

00:20:56.535 --> 00:21:01.176
What was it? / I do not know anymore.

00:21:01.216 --> 00:21:03.336
I have no idea at all. / Who was it?

00:21:03.336 --> 00:21:08.157
Ah, seriously? / It was when she said she
was 19, right?

00:21:08.217 --> 00:21:13.097
Right. / And she did not even say
forty-six.

00:21:13.157 --> 00:21:14.157
Ah!

00:21:14.737 --> 00:21:20.978
First Stage over.

00:21:20.978 --> 00:21:21.978
Wait, what?

00:21:26.899 --> 00:21:30.279
I have no idea what happened.

00:21:30.559 --> 00:21:34.260
You have advanced to the Second Stage. /
Congratulations.

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.420
So it was these two. / All right, all
right, all right.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.420
So that stage is over now, right?

00:21:37.640 --> 00:21:41.080
When you asked Michopa, “How many NGs was
it again?” had you already figured it out? / Yeah.

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:43.481
That is terrifying! / Wow, that is
terrifying!

00:21:43.881 --> 00:21:46.441
You had figured it out? / I just happened
to catch it.

00:21:46.801 --> 00:21:48.641
There was actually a moment for that? /
Did Ueda figure it out too?

00:21:49.081 --> 00:21:51.602
Wait, does everyone know now? / I still do
not get it at all.

00:21:51.702 --> 00:21:53.002
Tell us. / That was close.

00:21:53.102 --> 00:21:55.362
That was close, Ueda. You got lucky. /
Lucky.

00:21:55.962 --> 00:22:01.463
Wow, at this timing... / We will now
reveal the three secret NGs from this stage.

00:22:01.603 --> 00:22:03.063
They are helping us out. / Thank god.

00:22:04.223 --> 00:22:05.943
Saying numbers. / That one, huh.

00:22:06.623 --> 00:22:08.383
Pointing. / Eating two or more pieces of
candy.

00:22:08.757 --> 00:22:09.971
Whoa, no way. / Ah, so that was not one.

00:22:10.504 --> 00:22:12.204
Making a fist pump. / Those were the
three.

00:22:12.204 --> 00:22:15.104
Whoa, that was close. / Seriously close.

00:22:15.264 --> 00:22:17.345
Wait, then... / Voice of Heaven...

00:22:17.645 --> 00:22:20.765
Please wait in the lounge until the Second
Stage begins. / So the NG was getting ignored?

00:22:20.965 --> 00:22:26.886
Getting ignored. No amateur chit-chat. / I
never would have guessed numbers at all.

00:22:26.886 --> 00:22:28.646
Me neither. / Not even close.

00:22:28.706 --> 00:22:31.606
If I had not noticed... / then I would
have said it a ton at the end. I totally said it.

00:22:31.606 --> 00:22:34.546
Becky really did not say it much. / But
she dodged forty-six.

00:22:35.347 --> 00:22:37.347
For Sakurazaka... / Yeah.

00:22:39.187 --> 00:22:41.067
Pure luck. / Total luck.

00:22:42.227 --> 00:22:45.148
So how was the First Stage? / It was over
in a flash.

00:22:47.568 --> 00:22:49.368
This was probably one of the quicker ones,
honestly.

00:22:49.628 --> 00:22:55.749
Once someone gets them to say a number,
the reactions from the people who know are hilarious.

00:22:55.989 --> 00:22:57.649
They just turn sideways like this.

00:22:58.009 --> 00:23:03.650
So noticing it is one thing, but being
good at making someone else say it too...

00:23:03.810 --> 00:23:05.950
surprisingly, Kano was really good at that
part too.

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:10.951
That full skill set. / But even though
Kasuga had noticed, he never went as far as baiting anyone.

00:23:10.951 --> 00:23:13.391
Right. / Yeah, Kasuga was all about
self-preservation.

00:23:13.951 --> 00:23:16.411
Yeah. / Like, he absolutely was not going
to stick his neck out.

00:23:19.222 --> 00:23:29.013
That is the way you play when you are
coming for the full five million.

00:23:34.833 --> 00:23:38.154
Exactly.

00:23:44.822 --> 00:23:45.902
Got it right. / Got it right.

00:23:46.662 --> 00:23:48.805
That is a great start, though. / Great
start.

00:23:48.862 --> 00:23:52.302
You are fine now. / Wow, everyone stopped
using them all at once.

00:23:52.302 --> 00:23:55.002
Nice. / Please look at the prize monitor.

00:23:55.002 --> 00:23:56.002
Huh? / Oh? Huh?

00:23:56.062 --> 00:23:57.882
It changes? Is that a thing? / Wait, why?

00:23:58.823 --> 00:24:03.643
Because you cleared one stage, one million
yen has been added to the prize pool. / Whoa!

00:24:03.703 --> 00:24:06.303
Man, that makes it even scarier. / What?!

00:24:06.353 --> 00:24:07.353
Is that not amazing? / Amazing.

00:24:08.123 --> 00:24:09.803
Now I am even more frustrated. /
Seriously?

00:24:10.303 --> 00:24:12.563
We also have good news for you. / Oh, good
news?

00:24:12.723 --> 00:24:13.723
What is it?

00:24:13.823 --> 00:24:15.083
By special allowance from the game
masters,

00:24:15.463 --> 00:24:19.823
we have prepared a prize-up challenge
where you can increase the prize money even more.

00:24:19.842 --> 00:24:20.984
A prize-up challenge? / I want to do it.

00:24:21.363 --> 00:24:22.583
A challenge? / Huh?

00:24:24.223 --> 00:24:26.524
Oh? Who is that? Someone’s mother? / Did
somebody’s mom show up?

00:24:27.044 --> 00:24:30.944
A chair? / They are getting so suspicious.

00:24:30.944 --> 00:24:31.944
Whoa. / Whoa.

00:24:32.444 --> 00:24:35.144
Hey, is this the person who took everyone
away earlier? / Everyone... ah, maybe.

00:24:36.564 --> 00:24:41.084
Now I am suspicious of everything. / Yeah,
but we got trapped by those people earlier too.

00:24:41.624 --> 00:24:42.384
Why a sheep? / A sheep.

00:24:42.384 --> 00:24:45.124
A sheep. / A butler and a sheep?

00:24:45.124 --> 00:24:45.784
Whoa! / Oh, that angle.

00:24:45.784 --> 00:24:46.544
Of course. / Of course.

00:24:46.544 --> 00:24:48.244
Huh? / With that hand?

00:24:48.324 --> 00:24:52.944
Huh? / I feel like they are going to guess
it right away.

00:24:53.064 --> 00:24:55.465
Seriously. / I did not think we would be
this close already.

00:24:57.405 --> 00:24:58.405
A child? / What do you mean?

00:24:58.405 --> 00:24:59.405
A child, right? / A wolf?

00:25:01.655 --> 00:25:02.655
Maybe a goat? / A goat?

00:25:02.985 --> 00:25:08.585
It is a goat. / This is a celebrity all of
you surely know.

00:25:09.905 --> 00:25:15.985
What? Huh? / If you can identify who it
is, one million yen will be added to the prize money. / Whoa!

00:25:16.105 --> 00:25:17.585
Wait, wait. / A celebrity?

00:25:17.585 --> 00:25:20.265
We have seen all of these... wait, just
from the look alone?

00:25:21.806 --> 00:25:26.906
If you ask the celebrity questions, they
will answer with yes-or-no gestures.

00:25:28.046 --> 00:25:30.786
Use those hints to figure out the correct
answer.

00:25:31.326 --> 00:25:37.806
You get one guess per question, and you
may ask up to five questions.

00:25:37.846 --> 00:25:40.106
This is nerve-racking. / As for our
special guest...

00:25:40.106 --> 00:25:44.346
Man, this is hard. / During this
challenge, are there no secret NGs?

00:25:44.986 --> 00:25:49.167
During this challenge, no secret NGs will
be in effect. / Ohhh!

00:25:50.027 --> 00:25:52.267
All right! / Thank god, thank god.

00:25:52.347 --> 00:25:54.927
Work together, okay? / Right, we should
cooperate on this one.

00:25:55.007 --> 00:25:59.527
Completely different from ten minutes ago.
/ The prize-up challenge begins now.

00:25:59.607 --> 00:26:02.887
What kind of question should we ask? /
That matters a lot.

00:26:02.987 --> 00:26:06.067
Well, we already know it is a woman. /
Yeah, definitely.

00:26:06.427 --> 00:26:09.147
What could it be? / Maybe someone where we
can even infer the casting level.

00:26:09.167 --> 00:26:12.007
Exactly. / From the scale of the show and
all that.

00:26:12.587 --> 00:26:14.547
I want to know what generation she is
from. / That part.

00:26:14.807 --> 00:26:19.508
Exactly. / Like whether she was a former
idol, whether she is married, things like that.

00:26:19.768 --> 00:26:21.548
Yeah, right, narrow it down there. /
Occupation too.

00:26:21.608 --> 00:26:23.248
No, occupation. / Occupation, right.

00:26:23.308 --> 00:26:26.748
Ah, got it. / We can look from behind too,
right?

00:26:26.968 --> 00:26:27.968
Yes. / That is allowed.

00:26:28.148 --> 00:26:30.968
That is allowed? / Hair about this long.

00:26:31.788 --> 00:26:34.348
This kind of thing makes me think I can
really guess it. Female for sure. / Female for sure.

00:26:34.768 --> 00:26:36.048
A ponytail. / They are letting us look up
close.

00:26:36.288 --> 00:26:39.488
The fact that it does not look dyed feels
kind of idol-ish. / Idol-ish.

00:26:39.568 --> 00:26:40.968
Really? / I have no clue at all.

00:26:41.008 --> 00:26:45.509
No idea at all. / But this is a show with
a budget.

00:26:46.409 --> 00:26:47.949
See? / You are factoring in the budget
now?

00:26:48.769 --> 00:26:53.349
Nobody else would think like that. / So
maybe someone like Minami Hamabe, a real lead-actress level person.

00:26:53.529 --> 00:26:57.669
Ah, an actress. / I feel like they cast
the kind of person you would say, “No way they got her.”

00:26:57.929 --> 00:26:59.469
I can see that. / Yeah, exactly.

00:26:59.789 --> 00:27:01.889
This is tough. / We have got to just ask
the first question already.

00:27:02.069 --> 00:27:03.109
Shall we? / Yeah.

00:27:03.329 --> 00:27:04.849
What do we start with? / Are you an
actress?

00:27:05.149 --> 00:27:07.609
Maybe. / “Are you an actress?” makes
sense.

00:27:07.609 --> 00:27:12.170
But if she is an artist who also acts... /
Would that still count as an actress?

00:27:12.370 --> 00:27:15.110
So, your main job. / Right, your main job.

00:27:15.410 --> 00:27:16.410
Main job. / Actress, then?

00:27:16.830 --> 00:27:19.310
Please ask your question. / Okay.

00:27:20.030 --> 00:27:23.990
Is your main profession acting? / Ah.

00:27:27.434 --> 00:27:29.554
See? / Right, okay.

00:27:29.694 --> 00:27:31.034
Got it. / Right, right, right.

00:27:31.094 --> 00:27:32.234
This is huge. / This is huge.

00:27:32.294 --> 00:27:34.915
That narrows it down a lot. / So she is
not an actress.

00:27:35.255 --> 00:27:39.595
Please answer who you think this celebrity
is. / Oh, right. We have to make one guess each time.

00:27:39.595 --> 00:27:40.595
Exactly. / Right.

00:27:41.395 --> 00:27:44.395
About this tall. / An actress...

00:27:44.395 --> 00:27:46.375
Whoever you just thought of, I thought the
same thing. / Can I say it?

00:27:46.375 --> 00:27:48.396
Mana Ashida. / Whoa, that is totally
possible. Super possible.

00:27:48.616 --> 00:27:50.116
No, she would not do her nails. / She
would not.

00:27:50.236 --> 00:27:51.616
No way she would. / Yellow nails too.

00:27:51.656 --> 00:27:53.456
No way she would. / No way she would.

00:27:53.456 --> 00:27:54.456
Absolutely not. / Not even glitter?

00:27:54.456 --> 00:27:57.576
No. / Ah, glitter maybe... no, wait, that
is just nail polish.

00:27:57.696 --> 00:27:59.397
We're close. / It looks freshly painted
too.

00:27:59.777 --> 00:28:00.997
See? / We are too close.

00:28:01.037 --> 00:28:02.717
Mana Ashida is still possible. / Totally
possible.

00:28:03.737 --> 00:28:05.417
Yeah, possible. / Her posture is really
good too.

00:28:05.557 --> 00:28:07.337
Why Mana Ashida? / We are close, though.

00:28:07.357 --> 00:28:08.857
Well, first off, she has a small face. /
True.

00:28:08.857 --> 00:28:12.938
True, and Kamishiraishi has this kind of
vibe too. / Similar.

00:28:13.058 --> 00:28:14.598
I see. / Should we take another shot
already?

00:28:14.828 --> 00:28:15.828
Let us do it. / Huh?

00:28:15.958 --> 00:28:18.958
Are you Mana Ashida?

00:28:22.328 --> 00:28:23.328
Ah, no. / No.

00:28:24.478 --> 00:28:25.859
Incorrect. / Damn it.

00:28:26.459 --> 00:28:28.479
Why, why Mana Ashida? / Huh?

00:28:29.369 --> 00:28:30.369
Huh? / Wait, why?

00:28:30.399 --> 00:28:31.919
Why? / Ueda!!

00:28:31.919 --> 00:28:34.059
Wow, that is lame. / Wait, wait.

00:28:34.119 --> 00:28:35.959
You went along with it. / She played along
with us.

00:28:36.399 --> 00:28:38.400
She went along with it? / Wait, if we get
it wrong, do we lose a hundred?

00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:40.580
So we really do need to be careful now. /
Exactly.

00:28:40.660 --> 00:28:43.980
That is why. / And worst-case, if we miss
all five, it drops to one million, right?

00:28:43.980 --> 00:28:44.720
Right. / What is left.

00:28:44.720 --> 00:28:46.940
Hold on. / Is that not brutal?

00:28:47.020 --> 00:28:49.500
That changes everything. / Wait, so it can
go down?

00:28:49.600 --> 00:28:52.041
Of course it can. Otherwise... / Yeah,
true.

00:28:52.041 --> 00:28:54.141
Fair point. / Man...

00:28:54.341 --> 00:28:57.361
You have four chances left. / Four
chances.

00:28:57.981 --> 00:29:00.341
Everyone. / I want some clue about the
name.

00:29:00.511 --> 00:29:01.511
Yeah, exactly. / Right.

00:29:01.601 --> 00:29:04.522
But how do you ask that in yes-or-no form?
/ Like whether the name has a voiced consonant in it.

00:29:05.462 --> 00:29:08.542
That. / Then we can rule out people like
Minami Hamabe altogether, right?

00:29:09.242 --> 00:29:11.582
Ohhh. / Nice.

00:29:11.982 --> 00:29:12.982
Nice. / Really good.

00:29:12.982 --> 00:29:14.062
Let's go with that. / Whether her name
has a voiced consonant.

00:29:14.102 --> 00:29:17.023
Does your name contain a voiced consonant?
/ Nice one.

00:29:17.023 --> 00:29:19.003
Can we really ask that? / Yeah, I think
so.

00:29:19.003 --> 00:29:20.783
This is a good one, right? / Are we going
with voiced consonants?

00:29:22.023 --> 00:29:25.803
Does your full name contain a voiced
consonant?

00:29:30.744 --> 00:29:33.324
Whoa, it does? / No, but that still helps.

00:29:33.324 --> 00:29:35.864
No, that really narrows it down. / So it
is not Kamishiraishi.

00:29:35.944 --> 00:29:37.384
Not Kamishiraishi. / And not Sairi Ito
either.

00:29:37.504 --> 00:29:38.824
Not her. / That cuts a lot out.

00:29:40.184 --> 00:29:40.844
An actress... / Could be.

00:29:40.844 --> 00:29:43.745
Then please answer who you think this
celebrity is. / Yes, please answer.

00:29:44.245 --> 00:29:46.045
Then should I go with Minami Hamabe? /
That does make sense.

00:29:46.085 --> 00:29:48.885
Got it. / We have to say something or the
room gets too tense.

00:29:49.525 --> 00:29:52.305
It will get too heavy. / Are you Minami
Hamabe?

00:29:53.205 --> 00:29:56.326
All right, what is it? / Ahhh, wrong.

00:29:57.706 --> 00:30:00.006
Incorrect. / This is bad.

00:30:00.166 --> 00:30:01.466
This is bad. / Whoa!

00:30:01.486 --> 00:30:03.686
Whoa! / It dropped!!

00:30:04.066 --> 00:30:05.646
This is bad. / Matsumaru...

00:30:05.666 --> 00:30:07.487
Sorry. / Maybe we should have followed
Matsumaru more there.

00:30:07.627 --> 00:30:09.927
As for Matsumaru... / No, no, no, no.

00:30:10.907 --> 00:30:14.887
For example, asking if the name has three
syllables... / Ah.

00:30:14.987 --> 00:30:16.747
Given name? / The given name.

00:30:16.947 --> 00:30:20.088
That would narrow it down. / No, wait,
first we should list actress names.

00:30:20.448 --> 00:30:24.328
List them up. / Then ask a question that
fits those candidates.

00:30:24.428 --> 00:30:26.508
Suzu Hirose. / Her sister.

00:30:26.888 --> 00:30:27.888
Alice Hirose. / Alice, maybe.

00:30:27.888 --> 00:30:29.948
Alice, maybe. / No voiced consonant there.

00:30:30.688 --> 00:30:33.149
That voiced-consonant question might
actually have been really good. / Yeah.

00:30:34.309 --> 00:30:40.269
It may narrow things down more than you
think. / If we get her from just these two questions, that is incredible.

00:30:40.269 --> 00:30:41.909
No, really, that'd be amazing. / We're
doing well, right?

00:30:42.929 --> 00:30:46.890
Main job is actress, and there is a voiced
consonant in the name. / So then...

00:30:46.990 --> 00:30:48.930
Still not narrow enough. / Unless she
used to be an idol.

00:30:48.930 --> 00:30:50.110
Ah. / Right, now...

00:30:51.010 --> 00:30:52.990
she became an actress. / Like Atsuko
Maeda.

00:30:53.090 --> 00:30:57.471
Right, yeah, if that is true, it narrows
things down a lot. / Ah, Atsuko Maeda.

00:30:58.551 --> 00:31:00.991
What kind of hairstyle does she have now?
/ True.

00:31:02.231 --> 00:31:04.671
There is a voiced consonant. / No, is she
really that small?

00:31:04.831 --> 00:31:07.731
No, I felt like she looked kind of
delicate. / I see.

00:31:08.411 --> 00:31:11.412
Have we co-starred with her before? / But
yeah, I thought she might be a little taller.

00:31:12.132 --> 00:31:15.292
If they tell us that, it might be obvious
who it is. / But it is supposed to be someone everybody knows.

00:31:18.312 --> 00:31:21.452
Wow, what are you even looking at right
now? / Please ask your third question.

00:31:21.452 --> 00:31:22.452
Her nails and stuff. / Third question.

00:31:24.533 --> 00:31:30.213
Here we go. / Were you formerly an idol?

00:31:31.233 --> 00:31:33.973
Like, “How are you doing?” or something. /
Ohhh!

00:31:35.594 --> 00:31:36.954
Ohhh! / This is huge, right?

00:31:37.054 --> 00:31:38.054
Huge. / That narrows it a lot.

00:31:38.054 --> 00:31:40.554
Wait, Acchan? / Could it be Acchan?

00:31:40.714 --> 00:31:41.814
Acchan. / Atsuko Maeda.

00:31:41.894 --> 00:31:44.134
Who else is there? / Yuko Oshima.

00:31:44.154 --> 00:31:46.634
Yuko Oshima. / But she is not doing idol
work anymore now.

00:31:46.974 --> 00:31:49.035
Voiced consonant. / Former idol is a big
clue.

00:31:49.035 --> 00:31:50.835
Yeah. / And the name has a voiced
consonant.

00:31:50.865 --> 00:31:51.865
Ah. / Morning Musume?

00:31:51.895 --> 00:31:54.395
Morning Musume. / Or maybe someone from
Nogizaka.

00:31:55.055 --> 00:31:56.595
A small-built Nogizaka member. / Ah, ah.

00:31:57.615 --> 00:32:00.996
Mai Shiraishi. / No, Shiraishi has no
voiced consonant.

00:32:00.996 --> 00:32:03.036
No voiced consonant. / How did we lose to
this person?

00:32:03.356 --> 00:32:05.376
This is really frustrating. / I am so
annoyed.

00:32:06.896 --> 00:32:08.976
We got totally played by her. / Seriously.

00:32:09.316 --> 00:32:11.836
Completely. / She kind of had that ditzy
persona.

00:32:11.836 --> 00:32:13.176
I do not know many of them. / Kawaei?

00:32:13.637 --> 00:32:14.877
Ah, no. / No voiced consonant there
either.

00:32:15.057 --> 00:32:16.897
I cannot remember names. / Could it still
be Acchan?

00:32:17.137 --> 00:32:19.657
Should we go with Atsuko Maeda? / Should
we just do it?

00:32:19.851 --> 00:32:20.923
Then let us do it. / Kazu-san.

00:32:21.437 --> 00:32:24.177
Maybe Atsuko Maeda. / I mean, who else is
left?

00:32:25.037 --> 00:32:26.638
Yeah. / What if this is wrong?

00:32:26.638 --> 00:32:29.938
Then we try again. / Shall we go?

00:32:31.998 --> 00:32:36.134
Are you... / Atsuko Maeda?

00:32:40.714 --> 00:32:45.595
What? No way! Whoa! / Whoa, amazing!

00:32:46.175 --> 00:32:51.175
Whoa, amazing! / Amazing!

00:32:51.735 --> 00:32:53.015
Amazing! / Amazing!

00:32:53.635 --> 00:32:54.535
Amazing! / Incredible!

00:32:54.535 --> 00:32:55.175
Amazing! / Incredible!

00:32:55.175 --> 00:32:56.455
Amazing! / Yes!

00:32:56.475 --> 00:32:57.756
Atsuko Maeda, wow! / Welcome!

00:32:57.796 --> 00:33:00.316
Whoa, amazing! / What?!

00:33:00.316 --> 00:33:01.316
Amazing! / Amazing!

00:33:02.476 --> 00:33:05.016
I cannot believe you got it. / Since you
guessed correctly,

00:33:05.016 --> 00:33:06.736
This is huge, right? / one million yen
will be added.

00:33:06.736 --> 00:33:08.093
That was fast, fast, fast. / Ten in a row.

00:33:08.916 --> 00:33:12.376
Ah, it is back, it is back, it is back. /
All right, all right, it is back.

00:33:12.717 --> 00:33:14.857
Back, back, back. / The money is flying
around fast.

00:33:15.177 --> 00:33:17.577
I am even more impressed by Maeda-san /
coming here for this.

00:33:17.577 --> 00:33:19.917
Like, “Acchan came on the show for this?”
/ Yeah.

00:33:20.737 --> 00:33:26.197
Thanks to flawless teamwork, / the five of
them arrived at the correct answer in just three questions.

00:33:28.058 --> 00:33:31.078
And now, right after / they just started
getting along...

00:33:31.238 --> 00:33:32.838
they go back to being enemies. / Enemies
again now.

00:33:32.938 --> 00:33:38.978
Yeah. / In the Second Stage, Atsuko Maeda
joins as an accomplice who will lure out NGs.

00:33:39.799 --> 00:33:41.657
She gets to trap all five of them? /
While knowing the NGs?!

00:33:42.258 --> 00:33:45.659
So she is going to be baiting them while
knowing the prompts. / Then this is where the strategy comes in.

00:33:45.699 --> 00:33:52.699
Whoa. / And for the Second Stage, we are
going to bring out a giant jump rope and have them try it.

00:33:53.739 --> 00:33:57.059
And as for the secret NGs... / What should
we do here, Ninomiya?

00:33:57.459 --> 00:33:59.460
Something where they mess up and go,
“Ahh!” maybe. / Yeah.

00:33:59.620 --> 00:34:02.000
Right, right. / Maybe if we build in
apologizing...

00:34:02.340 --> 00:34:03.820
Yeah. / then nobody apologizes and...

00:34:04.460 --> 00:34:06.420
we get the worst jump-rope game ever. /
Apologizing...

00:34:07.260 --> 00:34:11.820
Apologizing has to be one, right? / If you
mess up and do not apologize, that is weird.

00:34:11.940 --> 00:34:13.881
It is weird. / Morally speaking, anyway.

00:34:14.161 --> 00:34:15.441
Yeah.

00:34:15.761 --> 00:34:19.241
The NGs they set are all things likely to
happen during a giant jump-rope game:

00:34:19.861 --> 00:34:23.201
apologizing, saying “don’t worry about
it,” and putting your hands on your knees.

00:34:23.201 --> 00:34:29.102
Who will be the first to notice the NGs,

00:34:30.412 --> 00:34:38.562
and switch over to attacking?

00:34:39.562 --> 00:34:44.663
Players, the game will now resume, so
please gather in the playroom.

00:34:50.263 --> 00:34:51.263
Huh? / Wait.

00:34:51.543 --> 00:34:53.463
Wait. / It changed.

00:34:54.303 --> 00:34:56.163
Wait. / It is a giant jump rope.

00:34:56.163 --> 00:34:56.883
What is this? / What?

00:34:56.883 --> 00:34:58.704
A giant jump rope? / There is space
cleared out.

00:34:58.704 --> 00:34:59.704
Suspicious. / Very suspicious.

00:35:00.484 --> 00:35:02.084
A rope? / We have prepared a giant jump
rope.

00:35:03.004 --> 00:35:04.004
A giant jump rope?

00:35:05.235 --> 00:35:13.645
All of you will take it on together. Fifty
jumps earns 500,000 yen, one hundred jumps earns one million, and the prize goes up every fifty jumps.

00:35:13.705 --> 00:35:15.585
A hundred, huh.

00:35:15.585 --> 00:35:20.985
However, if you fail to reach fifty, the
prize money will be cut in half. / What?!

00:35:20.985 --> 00:35:24.345
What?! / Then we absolutely have to clear
fifty.

00:35:24.525 --> 00:35:26.565
Then maybe we should not do it. / Is that
not hard?

00:35:27.145 --> 00:35:29.806
Yeah. / In this stage, this person will
also be joining you.

00:35:29.966 --> 00:35:31.226
Huh? / No way.

00:35:32.006 --> 00:35:33.526
No way. / Wait, what?

00:35:33.586 --> 00:35:35.306
Those boots. / Those boots?

00:35:36.406 --> 00:35:37.186
Whoa! / Ah, the boots, the boots.

00:35:37.186 --> 00:35:39.486
She is doing everything. / Excuse me for
joining you.

00:35:39.626 --> 00:35:41.706
I will be participating with you all. /
Please do.

00:35:41.946 --> 00:35:47.887
Please take care of us. / Maeda-san knows
every secret NG that is about to be set.

00:35:48.307 --> 00:35:49.027
What? / Wait, wait.

00:35:49.027 --> 00:35:50.427
No way. / So while we are doing this...

00:35:50.647 --> 00:35:53.227
she is going to lure us into them? / They
all hated her instantly.

00:35:54.447 --> 00:35:58.427
We have to deal with NGs and still clear
the jump-rope challenge. / Let us do it.

00:35:58.828 --> 00:36:00.368
Whoa. / Wow, this is wild.

00:36:00.671 --> 00:36:02.385
Wait, she's totally the enemy. / It hasn't
started yet, right?

00:36:03.628 --> 00:36:10.468
Maeda-san, could you help make it look
like we are all on the same team with a quick “Go team!” or something?

00:36:10.568 --> 00:36:11.888
A team chant, please.

00:36:11.948 --> 00:36:17.209
All right, for now let us all make a
circle together. / I do not feel like doing that at all.

00:36:17.309 --> 00:36:18.629
Everyone, gather up. / Okay.

00:36:18.629 --> 00:36:20.486
Wait, has it already started? / It is
fine, it is fine.

00:36:20.649 --> 00:36:22.469
It is fine, yes. / Here we go, yes.

00:36:22.669 --> 00:36:24.189
Everyone, hands together. / It has not
started yet, right?

00:36:24.189 --> 00:36:25.609
Wait, has it started? / It has, right?

00:36:25.609 --> 00:36:29.190
Okay, gather up. / Wait, are we trusting
her?

00:36:30.490 --> 00:36:32.610
It is fine. / Wait, it has not started
yet, right?

00:36:32.610 --> 00:36:33.610
Yes. / Hands together.

00:36:34.800 --> 00:36:35.800
Hands together.

00:36:40.950 --> 00:36:47.911
Ready? / Let us do this. Go team!

00:36:47.931 --> 00:36:50.811
Nobody says anything. / Three secret NGs
have been set.

00:36:51.831 --> 00:36:55.752
Second Stage, begin. / Ah, right.

00:36:55.772 --> 00:36:56.772
Glad we said it. / This is terrifying.

00:36:56.772 --> 00:36:59.992
Yeah. / Ah, that scared me.

00:37:00.272 --> 00:37:05.033
That is what happens, though. / Maeda-san,
are you turning the rope or jumping?

00:37:05.033 --> 00:37:06.673
You should be jumping. / Either is fine by
me.

00:37:07.813 --> 00:37:11.894
I think it is better if you jump. Fifty
will be tiring. / Kasuga and I will turn it.

00:37:11.894 --> 00:37:13.654
Yeah, let us do that. / Ah, right, you
have stamina.

00:37:13.654 --> 00:37:15.014
You have stamina. / Then shall we jump?

00:37:15.114 --> 00:37:16.214
Shall we jump? / Yeah.

00:37:17.314 --> 00:37:22.655
No way messing up on the rope itself is
the NG, right? / Yeah, right.

00:37:22.655 --> 00:37:23.655
Maybe let us first see about... / Hm?

00:37:25.095 --> 00:37:29.296
Is it really okay to just start jumping? /
Maeda-san, everyone should probably stretch first.

00:37:29.296 --> 00:37:32.656
Can we first check the speed of the rope?
/ Everyone should stretch once first.

00:37:33.716 --> 00:37:36.956
Jumping right away seems dangerous. /
Right.

00:37:37.657 --> 00:37:40.697
Dangerous, dangerous. / You should stretch
your Achilles tendon first.

00:37:40.697 --> 00:37:42.677
No, seriously, if something happens it
could be dangerous. / It is fine.

00:37:42.677 --> 00:37:44.477
I am fine. I am only turning the rope. /
Me too.

00:37:45.017 --> 00:37:50.038
Ah, so nobody is doing it after all. They
think it is bait. / Yeah.

00:37:50.098 --> 00:37:53.158
As much as possible... / Should we stand
closer together?

00:37:53.718 --> 00:37:56.259
I am honestly really scared. / Ah, then
great.

00:37:56.499 --> 00:37:57.999
Maybe we should be facing this way... /
Wait...

00:37:58.399 --> 00:38:00.839
Ah, but if we do that... / Ah, sorry.
Depends how we do it.

00:38:00.939 --> 00:38:03.859
Depends on the timing. / Could you give us
some kind of chant as a signal?

00:38:08.060 --> 00:38:09.060
Ah, sorry.

00:38:11.300 --> 00:38:17.581
One player triggered an NG.

00:38:21.832 --> 00:38:32.623
All right, everybody, think...

00:38:32.783 --> 00:38:34.983
Think through every move you just made.

00:38:35.297 --> 00:38:36.369
No, I do not get it. / What did I do?

00:38:36.443 --> 00:38:40.224
Because she knows how this game works. / I
am like, what did I do just now? What was it?

00:38:40.224 --> 00:38:43.324
Where? Who was it? That is where everyone
is now. / “Sorry” came out.

00:38:43.524 --> 00:38:47.144
If it goes off at this timing, I lose the
thread completely. / I have no idea.

00:38:47.304 --> 00:38:49.165
What? / Everybody, think.

00:38:50.005 --> 00:38:51.785
Because she already knows the game. / That
has to be it.

00:38:52.825 --> 00:38:55.205
Anyway, let us make Maeda-san say “Let us
do our best.” / Yeah.

00:38:55.505 --> 00:39:01.846
“Anyway, let us do our best. Go team!”
please. / All right then, everyone...

00:39:02.166 --> 00:39:05.886
Right, anyway, let us do our best. Okay. /
Ready, go team!

00:39:06.867 --> 00:39:10.467
Yeah. / Everyone keeps looking down now.

00:39:10.487 --> 00:39:14.047
They will not play along. / And she is our
guest too.

00:39:14.047 --> 00:39:14.988
Exactly. / Do not ignore her.

00:39:14.988 --> 00:39:19.008
The silence is kind of scary. Really
scary. / So maybe it is the chant after all.

00:39:22.268 --> 00:39:25.109
Huh? / We will now check whether an NG has
been triggered.

00:39:25.609 --> 00:39:27.669
Among the members... / Everyone, please
wait a moment.

00:39:28.069 --> 00:39:29.629
Just now, even more... / This is scary.

00:39:29.629 --> 00:39:33.830
So that means someone said even more? /
What did they say?

00:39:34.150 --> 00:39:39.718
They stacked it? / Sorry.

00:39:41.458 --> 00:39:45.338
They definitely said it. / Definitely said
it.

00:39:45.338 --> 00:39:50.159
Now that you look closely. / The judges
are watching really closely.

00:39:51.019 --> 00:39:52.959
One player triggered an NG. / Sorry.

00:39:55.559 --> 00:40:00.279
That makes two times now. / Everyone,
please return to your private rooms once more.

00:40:00.439 --> 00:40:05.140
Fast, fast, fast. / Man, that was
unexpected.

00:40:06.220 --> 00:40:08.520
That was unexpected. / Twice before we
even jumped.

00:40:08.580 --> 00:40:13.440
Becky is going out at this rate. / But I
am definitely on my first one.

00:40:13.940 --> 00:40:20.301
Right after I was mumbling, it went off. /
You said, “I don’t know,” right?

00:40:20.821 --> 00:40:25.001
Ah, “I don’t know,” huh. / The fact you
are focusing on yourself means you have some idea.

00:40:26.081 --> 00:40:29.701
If I had to guess... / I was thinking “if
I had to guess.”

00:40:30.642 --> 00:40:32.702
Like, “let’s try it.” / Ah.

00:40:33.622 --> 00:40:35.762
Or, “let’s do it.” / Ah, so positive
language.

00:40:37.082 --> 00:40:39.762
By the way, how are you finding
Maeda-san’s presence? / Honestly, she is a huge nuisance.

00:40:40.022 --> 00:40:43.682
Do not say that. / She is our guest.

00:40:44.362 --> 00:40:47.063
I cannot play along. / I cannot play along
with anything.

00:40:47.743 --> 00:40:52.303
Adding Acchan changed everything, and
everyone refusing whatever Acchan suggests...

00:40:52.983 --> 00:40:55.803
I think the game masters could easily have
predicted that.

00:40:57.003 --> 00:40:59.023
So for example... / apologizing.

00:40:59.904 --> 00:41:02.824
Maybe saying “sorry” is an NG. / That
would be wild.

00:41:03.944 --> 00:41:09.124
They are guessing everything. / They are
really analyzing the structure of the game.

00:41:10.144 --> 00:41:12.404
Hmm. / I have three candidate patterns.

00:41:14.005 --> 00:41:16.285
The first was... / “Ready...”

00:41:17.565 --> 00:41:20.065
Ah, that was good too. / The second was...

00:41:20.805 --> 00:41:23.925
The chant. / The chant.

00:41:24.425 --> 00:41:28.245
And the third is, since Acchan kept
wanting us to do the “Go team!” thing,

00:41:29.346 --> 00:41:31.406
maybe raising your hands is a loss too. /
Ah.

00:41:33.026 --> 00:41:37.806
Wow, you have every single one wrong. /
But the way you say it sounds so cool.

00:41:37.806 --> 00:41:40.606
The phrasing is cool, though. / He figured
it out.

00:41:40.606 --> 00:41:42.446
Ohhh. / He really is strong.

00:41:42.586 --> 00:41:47.587
So it was true after all. / Yeah.

00:41:47.727 --> 00:41:52.127
He has figured it out. / It is pointing.

00:41:52.327 --> 00:41:57.167
Everybody sure loves pointing. / Everyone,
please return to the playroom.

00:41:59.808 --> 00:42:02.908
Welcome back. / Acchan really is good at
this.

00:42:03.228 --> 00:42:05.088
She is. / The game resumes.

00:42:05.128 --> 00:42:07.748
She is good. / Right, everyone sees her as
a nuisance now.

00:42:08.148 --> 00:42:10.268
Let us make a circle one more time. / The
circle.

00:42:10.328 --> 00:42:11.348
Okay, okay. / Put your hands out.

00:42:11.548 --> 00:42:13.049
I am not putting my hands out. / I knew
they liked this one.

00:42:13.289 --> 00:42:15.029
Okay. / Shall we do it?

00:42:15.609 --> 00:42:17.909
Let us do it, let us do it. / Now the
question is whether Ueda raises his hands too.

00:42:17.909 --> 00:42:18.989
Right. / All right, let us do this.

00:42:20.169 --> 00:42:24.629
Go, go, team! / He is not raising them,
not raising them.

00:42:24.709 --> 00:42:27.330
Let us go. / Nobody says anything.

00:42:27.330 --> 00:42:31.730
Ueda Tatsuya is not raising his hands. /
Wouldn’t it be better if we stood closer together?

00:42:31.730 --> 00:42:36.950
No, because then it turns into, “Ah, ah,
ah, ah...” / and we might kick each other in the shins.

00:42:37.030 --> 00:42:41.030
Yeah. / What exactly is everyone being
careful about now?

00:42:41.170 --> 00:42:42.831
I cannot do anything. / Let us do it.

00:42:43.431 --> 00:42:44.431
Okay. / All right.

00:42:44.641 --> 00:42:45.641
Let us do our best. / Yeah.

00:42:46.951 --> 00:42:50.411
So Kano has dropped “let’s do it” and
“let’s try it” now. / I see.

00:42:50.771 --> 00:42:53.111
He tested them out. / He was listening for
them.

00:42:54.191 --> 00:42:56.012
This is hard. / So right now, everyone is
basically...

00:42:56.012 --> 00:42:57.012
Ready...

00:42:58.052 --> 00:43:03.652
How about Mukai and Kasuga, are they
trying to bait people?

00:43:03.812 --> 00:43:10.192
Kano is kind of dangerous now. / Kano
really is.

00:43:10.192 --> 00:43:13.833
Ah, what happens now? / Wait, what, what,
what?

00:43:13.893 --> 00:43:14.893
What happens? / I hate this.

00:43:15.133 --> 00:43:16.133
Who? Who? / Huh?

00:43:17.553 --> 00:43:20.773
I actually jumped pretty well. / Yeah.

